---
globs:
  - "src/**/*.ts"
  - ".env.example"
  - "docs/configuration.md"
---

Every tunable has one home, catalogued in `docs/configuration.md`. Env-backed knob: name in `ENV` (`src/settings/envKeys.ts`), default in `src/settings/defaults.ts`, parse in `loadConfig` (`src/config.ts`), a line in `.env.example`, a row in `docs/configuration.md`; `test/settingsInventory.test.ts` fails when `.env.example` and `ENV` drift. Code constant: a `src/settings/` constants module such as `reviewConstants.ts`, re-exported by `constants.ts`, plus a row under Code constants. Import through `../settings/index.js`. Take `Config` only at runtime entry points (`src/index.ts`, `src/worker.ts`) and pass values down. Flag a new literal timeout, byte cap, count, queue name, marker string, or user-facing sentence sitting in a feature module; compare `CODE_MODE_*`, `TRIAGE_*`, `VERIFICATION_STUB_MARKER`. Flag a `process.env` read outside `src/config.ts`, `codeModeConstants.ts`, `modelsJsonCatalog.ts`, `evlog.ts`, and `NODE_ENV` test guards, and any default duplicating `defaults.ts`.
